Class Responsibility <code>Session</code> Single server connection state: nick, channels, capabilities <code>SessionManager</code> Manages sessions, routes events, command processing <code>Channel</code> Per-channel state: ring buffer, nick list, topic, modes <code>UserEntry</code> Nick + modes + host + away + account + realname <code>MessageHistory</code> Ring buffer (circular array) with scroll position <code>HighlightRules</code> Pattern matching for highlights (regex + word boundary) <code>IgnoreList</code> Hostmask patterns with wildcard support <code>AutoAway</code> Auto-away on background, back on foreground <code>ServiceIdentify</code> NickServ/ChanServ identification <code>WhoisCache</code> Cached whois results with TTL <code>CommandProcessor</code> Parses <code>/commands</code>, dispatches to handlers <code>IrcCase</code> Case-insensitive comparison per RFC 1459 <p>Channel Ring Buffer: <pre><code>// MessageHistory.java
private final String[] buffer = new String[capacity];
private int head = 0;
private int size = 0;
private int scrollOffset = 0;  // 0 = at bottom (live)
</code></pre> - O(1) append, O(1) random access for rendering - Scroll offset preserved across channel switches</p>

Class Record Store Data <code>ProfileStore</code> <code>chatterbox-profile-&lt;name&gt;</code> All connection settings <code>SettingsStore</code> <code>chatterbox-settings</code> Global UI prefs, highlights, ignore <code>LogStore</code> <code>chatterbox-log-&lt;server&gt;</code> Persistent scrollback (1000 lines/channel) <code>IgnoreStore</code> <code>chatterbox-ignore</code> Ignore masks <p>RMS Patterns: <pre><code>// ProfileStore.save(Profile p)
RecordStore rs = RecordStore.openRecordStore(name, true);
byte[] data = serialize(p);  // DataOutputStream → ByteArrayOutputStream
if (rs.getNumRecords() == 0) rs.addRecord(data, 0, data.length);
else rs.setRecord(1, data, 0, data.length);
rs.closeRecordStore();
</code></pre></p>

Thread Responsibility Main (MIDlet) LCDUI event dispatch, <code>commandAction()</code>, <code>paint()</code> Connection I/O One per connection: <code>Connection.run()</code> blocking read Timer/Keepalive <code>TimerTask</code> for PING, reconnect backoff RMS Synchronous on calling thread (fast, small data) <p>Thread Safety: - <code>SessionManager</code> / <code>Channel</code> / <code>MessageHistory</code> — Not thread-safe - All mutations from network thread → <code>Display.callSerially(() → mutate + repaint)</code> - <code>FloodQueue</code> — Synchronized (producer: UI thread, consumer: network thread)</p> <pre><code>// Typical pattern in ConnectionManager
Display.getDisplay(midlet).callSerially(() -&gt; {
    session.handleMessage(msg);
    chatView.repaint();
});
</code></pre>
